From 43db5bab36f88e39e2d352708af7f811c7a00392 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:34:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat(library-solidity): FHE.isAccountRetired for
 applications (lifecycle Level 2, Profile A)

Next to FHE.isAccountDenied, through Impl and IACL, in the codegen
templates and the four generated library files (library-solidity and
host-contracts copies, identical blocks). Applications use it to refuse
identity-gated grants made on behalf of a retired account.

The helper requires an ACL with the lifecycle Core: against an older ACL
the call reverts, so a Profile A gate fails closed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host-contracts/lib/FHE.sol                     |  8 ++++++++
 host-contracts/lib/Impl.sol                    | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../codegen/src/templates/FHE.sol-template     |  8 ++++++++
 .../codegen/src/templates/Impl.sol-template    | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 library-solidity/lib/FHE.sol                   |  8 ++++++++
 library-solidity/lib/Impl.sol                  | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 78 insertions(+)

diff --git a/host-contracts/lib/FHE.sol b/host-contracts/lib/FHE.sol
index 9ec69ff8..2eff1759 100644
--- a/host-contracts/lib/FHE.sol
+++ b/host-contracts/lib/FHE.sol
@@ -8165,6 +8165,14 @@ library FHE {
         return Impl.isAccountDenied(account);
     }
 
+    /**
+     * @dev Returns whether the account is retired (decryption authority lifecycle). Retirement is one-way.
+     *      Applications use it to refuse identity-gated grants made on behalf of a retired account (Profile A).
+     */
+    function isAccountRetired(address account) internal view returns (bool) {
+        return Impl.isAccountRetired(account);
+    }
+
     /// @notice Checks if the `handle` can be decrypted in the given context (`user`, `contractAddress`).
     /// @param handle The handle as a bytes32.
     /// @param user The account address that is part of the user decryption context.
